# YouTube Download Refactor (Sept 2025)

## Summary
A unified helper `backend/utils/youtube.py` now centralizes:
- Video ID extraction (`extract_video_id`)
- URL normalization (`normalize_url`)
- Downloading via yt-dlp (`download_video`) returning a structured `DownloadResult`.

## Migrated Components
- `generator_refactored.py` now delegates ID extraction & download.
- `generator.py` (legacy) delegates `extract_video_id` when utility available.
- `processor.py` download logic replaced with a thin wrapper around the unified utility while preserving its `(path, title)` return shape.

## Rationale
Previously multiple modules duplicated:
- Regex patterns for video ID extraction
- Large verbose yt-dlp option dictionaries
- Ad-hoc retry/error handling

This increased maintenance cost and risk of inconsistent YouTube breakage handling.

## Behavior Changes
- Default download now caps quality selection to <=1080p (can be extended later) for faster, predictable processing.
- Reduced logging noise; still prints basic resolution/duration summary.
- Retry logic standardized (3 attempts, small backoff).

## Future Enhancements (Recommended)
1. Add optional env var `YOUTUBE_MAX_HEIGHT` to allow 1440p/2160p downloads when desired.
2. Introduce simple file cache (skip re-download if file already exists & size > 0).
3. Centralize availability checks (private/premium/live) inside utility (currently minimal).
4. Add unit tests for `backend/utils/youtube.py` with mocked yt_dlp.
5. Replace legacy direct calls in any remaining modules (search for `download_video(` outside utility for drift).
6. Add structured logging (JSON) for download telemetry.

